      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the comments. The path was following. The context switch happened from onScannerRegistered() callback.\n\n```\nstartScanForIntent() -\u003e registerPiAndStartScan() -\u003e onScannerRegistered() callback -\u003e continuePiStartScan() -\u003e new ScanClient() -\u003e Binder.getCallingUid();\n```\n\nIf not tracking the original caller uid for Pending Intent, I\u0027m not sure which uid has to be checked for optimizing scan parameters. In b/299231195, the 3P app started 100% duty cycle scan by Pending Intent and the scan was not downgraded even during screen off because the caller was btservice stying foreground forever.",
